1
00:00:42,647 --> 00:00:46,067
SOLD OUT ON YOU

2
00:00:50,905 --> 00:00:51,865
<i>Do you want perfection?</i>

3
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:55,702
<i>Then, don't stand by my side.</i>

4
00:00:55,785 --> 00:00:56,828
Do you want perfection?

5
00:00:56,911 --> 00:00:58,621
Then, don't stand by my side.

6
00:00:58,705 --> 00:00:59,622
INSTANT CURRY

7
00:00:59,706 --> 00:01:01,457
<i>Say "Ah."</i>

8
00:01:01,541 --> 00:01:02,458
<i>It's so delicious.</i>

9
00:01:02,542 --> 00:01:04,961
<i>No need to worry about tonight's dinner!</i>

10
00:01:05,044 --> 00:01:07,088
No need to worry about tonight's dinner!

11
00:01:08,256 --> 00:01:09,257
EUNSUNG SUPER VACUUM

12
00:01:10,633 --> 00:01:12,552
<i>-You're a lifesaver.</i>
-You're a lifesaver.

13
00:01:37,327 --> 00:01:38,578
Mom…

14
00:01:38,661 --> 00:01:39,537
Ye-jin!

15
00:01:40,538 --> 00:01:43,249
Ye-jin, are you okay? Are you hurt?

16
00:01:43,958 --> 00:01:45,084
Mom…

17
00:01:47,921 --> 00:01:49,464
Dad,

18
00:01:49,547 --> 00:01:52,050
this person is my mom, right?

19
00:01:53,301 --> 00:01:54,427
Is it?

20
00:01:54,510 --> 00:01:57,055
Is she really my mom?

21
00:01:59,015 --> 00:02:00,016
Mom!

22
00:02:00,099 --> 00:02:02,018
<i>It's me, Dam Seok-gyeong.</i>

23
00:02:02,101 --> 00:02:04,646
<i>Ye-jin's having a hard time.</i>

24
00:02:04,729 --> 00:02:06,147
<i>Can you meet her just once?</i>

25
00:02:13,404 --> 00:02:14,656
Ye-jin.

26
00:02:17,242 --> 00:02:18,284
It's me, your mom.

27
00:02:19,327 --> 00:02:20,245
Come here.

28
00:02:24,165 --> 00:02:25,667
Mom!

29
00:02:29,337 --> 00:02:32,882
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

30
00:02:45,186 --> 00:02:46,896
-How is it? Is it good?
-It's good.

31
00:03:11,212 --> 00:03:12,255
Mom.

32
00:03:13,589 --> 00:03:17,301
Can't we play outside next time?

33
00:03:18,553 --> 00:03:19,429
What?

34
00:03:20,304 --> 00:03:23,516
I want to go
to an amusement park with you.

35
00:03:24,851 --> 00:03:25,852
Well…

36
00:03:26,728 --> 00:03:28,688
-I'm really busy--
-Then…

37
00:03:29,772 --> 00:03:31,816
When can I see you again?

38
00:03:40,575 --> 00:03:41,576
Ye-jin.

39
00:03:42,118 --> 00:03:44,120
This is my number.

40
00:03:44,746 --> 00:03:47,206
You can call me at this number
when you miss me.

41
00:03:47,707 --> 00:03:48,541
Really?

42
00:03:48,624 --> 00:03:53,171
But can you promise me
just one thing in return?

43
00:03:54,005 --> 00:03:57,091
Until I come to see you,

44
00:03:58,009 --> 00:04:00,720
promise to never come looking for me.

45
00:04:08,311 --> 00:04:09,312
Because--

46
00:04:09,395 --> 00:04:11,189
Because it's our secret.

47
00:04:19,947 --> 00:04:22,033
Can I call you every day?

48
00:04:23,451 --> 00:04:25,495
Right, you're busy.

49
00:04:26,829 --> 00:04:29,707
Then, how about this?

50
00:04:30,249 --> 00:04:32,502
Every Sunday night at 8:00 p.m.,

51
00:04:32,585 --> 00:04:35,922
<i>no matter how busy I am,</i>
<i>I promise to pick up.</i>

52
00:04:36,005 --> 00:04:37,590
<i>Hey, Ye-jin.</i>

53
00:04:37,673 --> 00:04:40,885
Mom, I became class president!
Everyone except three people voted for me.

54
00:04:42,011 --> 00:04:43,054
Congratulations!

55
00:04:51,896 --> 00:04:54,065
EUN-SU'S LAW

56
00:04:54,148 --> 00:04:57,860
COMMENT
SONG MYEONG-HWA'S ACTING IS AMAZING!

57
00:04:58,945 --> 00:05:00,238
MOM

58
00:05:02,198 --> 00:05:04,200
Mom, do you finally get
your revenge tomorrow?

59
00:05:04,826 --> 00:05:06,160
Can't you tell just me?

60
00:05:06,244 --> 00:05:08,454
It's more fun if you watch it yourself.

61
00:05:09,956 --> 00:05:10,998
Ms. Song.

62
00:05:11,499 --> 00:05:12,458
They need me.

63
00:05:13,042 --> 00:05:15,378
-<i>Let's talk more next week.</i>
-Okay.

64
00:05:15,461 --> 00:05:16,546
I love you--

65
00:05:26,347 --> 00:05:28,891
<i>The person you are calling is unavailable.</i>

66
00:05:34,814 --> 00:05:38,067
-Gosh, Song Myeong-hwa got in an accident.
-Really? What happened?

67
00:05:43,364 --> 00:05:45,533
SONG MYEONG-HWA
IN CRITICAL CONDITION AFTER CAR CRASH

68
00:06:03,259 --> 00:06:05,303
Correct that false report first.

69
00:06:05,386 --> 00:06:07,138
-Ms. Song Myeong-hwa!
-Ms. Song Myeong-hwa!

70
00:06:07,221 --> 00:06:08,806
How did the accident occur?

71
00:06:08,890 --> 00:06:10,266
What happened to the others?

72
00:06:10,349 --> 00:06:11,267
Mom!

73
00:06:16,022 --> 00:06:17,356
Do you know this kid?

74
00:06:21,319 --> 00:06:22,361
I mean…

75
00:06:22,445 --> 00:06:24,030
You can't just let anyone in here!

76
00:06:25,406 --> 00:06:27,491
Sorry. She needs to rest right now.

77
00:06:31,495 --> 00:06:33,664
-Please leave right now!
-Song Myeong-hwa!

78
00:06:34,707 --> 00:06:37,126
Mom, I'm sorry.

79
00:06:38,169 --> 00:06:40,338
Please, just pick up.

80
00:06:43,341 --> 00:06:45,551
Mom, please answer the phone.

81
00:06:47,803 --> 00:06:48,638
Just once…

82
00:06:48,721 --> 00:06:51,682
<i>The person you are calling is unavailable.</i>
<i>Please leave a message…</i>

83
00:06:51,766 --> 00:06:53,100
Just once…

84
00:06:54,185 --> 00:06:55,186
Mom.

85
00:06:57,772 --> 00:06:59,649
Why weren't you picking up?

86
00:07:12,578 --> 00:07:14,121
Are you listening?

87
00:07:18,876 --> 00:07:20,461
You've called the wrong number.

88
00:07:27,510 --> 00:07:28,761
Hello?

89
00:07:30,555 --> 00:07:31,681
Hello?

90
00:07:59,083 --> 00:08:00,167
<i>Mom?</i>

91
00:08:02,253 --> 00:08:04,463
-Mom.
<i>-If you call me one more time,</i>

92
00:08:04,547 --> 00:08:06,382
I'm going to call the cops.

93
00:08:06,465 --> 00:08:08,009
This is my last warning.

94
00:08:52,386 --> 00:08:54,055
-Look here.
-<i>I miss you.</i>

95
00:08:59,226 --> 00:09:01,020
I miss you,

96
00:09:03,397 --> 00:09:04,523
Mom.

97
00:10:00,329 --> 00:10:01,205
SOM'S VARIETY SHOP

98
00:10:01,288 --> 00:10:02,373
Jin-yi!

99
00:10:02,456 --> 00:10:05,960
It seems our regulars
are here early this morning.

100
00:10:06,043 --> 00:10:08,129
Hey, Jin-yi. My stool, please.

101
00:10:08,212 --> 00:10:11,048
-A stool for me too.
-Your stools!

102
00:10:11,674 --> 00:10:12,717
All right.

103
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:15,678
-A high one for you.
-A high one.

104
00:10:15,761 --> 00:10:17,930
And a low one for you.

105
00:10:18,013 --> 00:10:19,223
Thank you.

106
00:10:19,306 --> 00:10:21,767
Don't share these
just because you're friends, okay?

107
00:10:21,851 --> 00:10:25,187
You need to use the right ones
for your heights to protect your knees.

108
00:10:26,522 --> 00:10:28,566
I want to buy a stool too.

109
00:10:29,316 --> 00:10:31,193
Let me hear Jin-yi nag about my knees.

110
00:10:31,944 --> 00:10:34,196
There's no need to buy one.

111
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:37,032
-Just give me one.
-Save your money.

112
00:10:37,783 --> 00:10:39,285
She's so considerate.

113
00:10:39,368 --> 00:10:41,954
Jin-yi is a true businesswoman.

114
00:10:42,037 --> 00:10:43,456
"The Cunning Dealer Jin-yi."

115
00:10:44,206 --> 00:10:46,375
-All right, let's go.
-Let's go.

116
00:10:46,459 --> 00:10:48,002
-We have to go now.
-Bye.

117
00:10:48,085 --> 00:10:51,380
-Let's go have some coffee.
-Let's go get coffee.

118
00:10:51,464 --> 00:10:52,298
Hey, Som-yi!

119
00:10:52,381 --> 00:10:54,675
Hang on! Come here.

120
00:10:55,926 --> 00:10:56,969
I don't want to.

121
00:10:57,636 --> 00:10:59,555
Let me see…

122
00:11:01,223 --> 00:11:02,099
All right.

123
00:11:02,641 --> 00:11:03,476
Wear this.

124
00:11:04,560 --> 00:11:05,603
What is this?

125
00:11:05,686 --> 00:11:09,607
It's a Punggi rayon mask
that I got just for you.

126
00:11:09,690 --> 00:11:11,650
It doesn't trap sweat,
and it's very breathable.

127
00:11:11,734 --> 00:11:13,360
It's so soft. Isn't it awesome?

128
00:11:13,444 --> 00:11:15,613
Forget it. I'll stick with what I have.

129
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:19,492
Five, four, three!

130
00:11:20,117 --> 00:11:21,494
Come on!

131
00:11:30,377 --> 00:11:31,212
What do you think?

132
00:11:33,547 --> 00:11:34,507
It's so-so.

133
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:37,718
Na Som-yi.

134
00:11:44,058 --> 00:11:45,184
No way!

135
00:11:45,267 --> 00:11:48,062
Jin-yi, this is what I really wanted!

136
00:11:48,145 --> 00:11:50,564
What kind of angel left this here for me?

137
00:11:50,648 --> 00:11:53,692
Who else would it be?
You begged Mechoori for it, didn't you?

138
00:11:54,485 --> 00:11:55,402
No, I didn't.

139
00:11:55,486 --> 00:11:58,822
I'm going to open this later,
so keep it safe for me.

140
00:12:02,576 --> 00:12:03,410
You're doing great.

141
00:12:35,651 --> 00:12:37,319
My eyes are a bit puffy.

142
00:12:37,987 --> 00:12:39,905
Did I eat too much soup last night?

143
00:12:44,076 --> 00:12:44,910
Goodness.

144
00:12:48,289 --> 00:12:49,373
Are you leaving?

145
00:12:49,456 --> 00:12:51,458
Yes. Are you heading out too?

146
00:12:51,542 --> 00:12:53,627
-Yeah, I'm going to the market.
-I see.

147
00:12:53,711 --> 00:12:55,963
Let's go together. I'm riding the bus too.

148
00:12:56,046 --> 00:12:57,673
Sure. I'll give you a ride there.

149
00:12:58,257 --> 00:13:01,051
-You drive?
-Of course not.

150
00:13:01,135 --> 00:13:04,597
There's someone who never lets me walk.

151
00:13:23,824 --> 00:13:25,868
Yeah, that's the one!

152
00:13:25,951 --> 00:13:29,580
This chicken was flying
like an eagle yesterday!

153
00:13:29,663 --> 00:13:30,998
You…

154
00:13:31,081 --> 00:13:33,959
You treated me like a thief
and even called the cops.

155
00:13:35,002 --> 00:13:38,130
But is that really a chicken though?

156
00:13:38,797 --> 00:13:40,633
I'm telling you, it's really weird.

157
00:13:45,596 --> 00:13:47,473
You don't have anything to say to me?

158
00:13:54,146 --> 00:13:55,356
Here.

159
00:14:02,404 --> 00:14:04,281
I wasn't asking for repair costs.
An apology--

160
00:14:04,365 --> 00:14:05,574
We're all done, right?

161
00:14:06,158 --> 00:14:08,202
I hope we don't cross paths again.

162
00:14:10,162 --> 00:14:11,664
Excuse me!

163
00:14:11,747 --> 00:14:12,915
What? What is it now?

164
00:14:14,458 --> 00:14:15,459
Let's talk.

165
00:14:16,919 --> 00:14:19,672
We're going to miss the bus! Let's go.

166
00:14:28,263 --> 00:14:30,516
You can't take out any of this stuff?

167
00:14:30,599 --> 00:14:33,018
No. I only have space to give you a ride.

168
00:14:34,395 --> 00:14:37,523
Then, she can sit on my lap.

169
00:14:37,606 --> 00:14:39,024
You got knee surgery last year.

170
00:14:39,108 --> 00:14:40,025
You can't do that.

171
00:14:41,235 --> 00:14:42,319
You should get on, ma'am.

172
00:14:42,403 --> 00:14:43,362
I'll just walk.

173
00:14:43,445 --> 00:14:44,947
Why don't you come with us?

174
00:14:45,030 --> 00:14:45,990
We're going to be late.

175
00:14:47,616 --> 00:14:49,201
My goodness.

176
00:14:53,455 --> 00:14:54,415
Just sit.

177
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:58,377
You look so good together.

178
00:14:58,460 --> 00:15:01,380
-Darling, do you have a boyfriend?
-Pardon?

179
00:15:01,463 --> 00:15:02,881
Ma'am!

180
00:15:02,965 --> 00:15:06,593
Gosh, my knees hurt. I better sit down.

181
00:15:13,100 --> 00:15:14,435
Put your feet up.

182
00:15:17,104 --> 00:15:18,105
Okay.

183
00:15:35,497 --> 00:15:37,082
Oh, my gosh!

184
00:15:37,166 --> 00:15:39,460
Bees! Mister, there are bees over here!

185
00:15:39,543 --> 00:15:40,586
Are they gone yet?

186
00:15:40,669 --> 00:15:42,212
Are they gone?

187
00:15:42,296 --> 00:15:43,422
They're gone.

188
00:15:48,927 --> 00:15:50,304
Why were they all over me?

189
00:15:52,473 --> 00:15:53,640
That's what I wanted to ask.

190
00:16:02,691 --> 00:16:05,152
I'm sorry
about yesterday's misunderstanding.

191
00:16:05,736 --> 00:16:07,071
I was too harsh.

192
00:16:09,198 --> 00:16:10,282
Well…

193
00:16:10,908 --> 00:16:13,786
I totally get it.

194
00:16:14,411 --> 00:16:15,412
Let's call it even.

195
00:16:16,246 --> 00:16:17,289
The envelope of money!

196
00:16:17,372 --> 00:16:19,875
I put it in the corner of your trailer,
so don't forget it.

197
00:16:19,958 --> 00:16:20,876
I don't need it.

198
00:16:21,460 --> 00:16:22,711
I don't need it either.

199
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:24,713
You said it was expensive.

200
00:16:24,797 --> 00:16:25,714
Please…

201
00:16:26,632 --> 00:16:27,716
Hey, I'm Dam Ye-jin.

202
00:17:16,390 --> 00:17:17,599
Dam Ye-jin?

203
00:17:23,480 --> 00:17:24,523
Hurry up.

204
00:17:31,905 --> 00:17:34,741
Ma'am, you can just pay later
when you get off.

205
00:17:34,825 --> 00:17:37,452
-It's not that…
-Geez.

206
00:17:37,536 --> 00:17:40,122
Aren't you hungry?
I bet you didn't have any breakfast.

207
00:17:40,205 --> 00:17:41,206
Eat this.

208
00:17:42,082 --> 00:17:43,917
It must be tough.

209
00:17:47,254 --> 00:17:50,424
Sang-geum, why would you give
that grumpy man any food?

210
00:18:15,324 --> 00:18:19,953
WE SPENT OUR TWENTIES TOGETHER

211
00:18:33,258 --> 00:18:34,509
Hey, Ae-ra!

212
00:18:41,892 --> 00:18:43,769
We met when we were eight,

213
00:18:44,561 --> 00:18:45,687
but now we're 40.

214
00:18:46,897 --> 00:18:47,856
Forty!

215
00:18:47,940 --> 00:18:49,524
We're "Young Forty"!

216
00:18:50,484 --> 00:18:51,693
Hey, Ae-ra.

217
00:18:51,777 --> 00:18:53,737
My next NeoTube video
is going to be called

218
00:18:53,820 --> 00:18:56,615
"Introducing Hidden Gems in our Town."

219
00:18:56,698 --> 00:18:59,993
And of course,
we can't be leaving you out.

220
00:19:00,077 --> 00:19:01,995
You were our student president,
valedictorian,

221
00:19:02,079 --> 00:19:03,956
and leader of the kids
in our neighborhood.

222
00:19:04,748 --> 00:19:06,250
Don't you have anything to do?

223
00:19:06,333 --> 00:19:08,710
I'll film a great clip of you
at that macaron place.

224
00:19:08,794 --> 00:19:09,670
What do you say?

225
00:19:11,171 --> 00:19:12,256
Come on. What do you say?

226
00:19:14,049 --> 00:19:15,926
How many subscribers did you say you have?

227
00:19:17,219 --> 00:19:18,470
Seven…

228
00:19:19,054 --> 00:19:20,389
subscribers.

229
00:19:22,975 --> 00:19:24,101
Will you do it if I get ten?

230
00:19:24,893 --> 00:19:26,061
-Are you crazy?
-Fifteen?

231
00:19:26,144 --> 00:19:27,938
-That's enough.
-Twenty?

232
00:19:29,147 --> 00:19:31,066
Born and raised in Deokpung,

233
00:19:31,149 --> 00:19:34,194
I'm Deokpung rep Park Kwang-mo,
and I'm here today to introduce

234
00:19:34,278 --> 00:19:37,239
these plastic bottle pinwheels.

235
00:19:37,322 --> 00:19:39,700
It's a budget-friendly mole repellent.

236
00:19:39,783 --> 00:19:41,159
When the wind blows,

237
00:19:41,243 --> 00:19:44,121
these bottles spin around,
and the vibrations go underground.

238
00:19:44,204 --> 00:19:48,083
The moles think
it's an earthquake and run off.

239
00:19:48,166 --> 00:19:49,751
It's very budget-friendly

240
00:19:49,835 --> 00:19:50,752
and easy to install--

241
00:19:50,836 --> 00:19:51,670
What's that?

242
00:19:53,714 --> 00:19:57,092
Right as I speak,
here comes our village's true gem.

243
00:19:57,175 --> 00:19:58,677
It's Mechoori.

244
00:20:00,304 --> 00:20:01,513
He's coming.

245
00:20:02,681 --> 00:20:04,266
He's still coming.

246
00:20:05,767 --> 00:20:07,519
He should stop coming now.

247
00:20:08,437 --> 00:20:10,147
To all the fans of Park Kwang-mo TV--

248
00:20:10,230 --> 00:20:11,398
Hey!

249
00:20:12,190 --> 00:20:13,483
Hey, Mechoori!

250
00:20:18,322 --> 00:20:21,408
You can't be drowsy driving
around the rice paddies.

251
00:20:22,617 --> 00:20:24,328
I didn't get enough sleep.

252
00:20:25,120 --> 00:20:28,040
Why? Was there a mosquito?

253
00:20:28,749 --> 00:20:31,501
It was something
more persistent than a mosquito.

254
00:20:32,127 --> 00:20:33,128
What?

255
00:20:34,504 --> 00:20:35,505
What are you saying?

256
00:20:35,589 --> 00:20:36,590
<i>Mom?</i>

257
00:20:37,841 --> 00:20:39,718
<i>Mom…</i>

258
00:20:42,012 --> 00:20:42,888
<i>Mom.</i>

259
00:20:44,348 --> 00:20:46,350
Just go and get some rest today.

260
00:20:46,850 --> 00:20:49,394
I'll take care of the farm.

261
00:20:50,062 --> 00:20:52,147
All right. I'd appreciate that.

262
00:20:52,230 --> 00:20:53,148
Sure.

263
00:21:04,159 --> 00:21:05,452
What is that?

264
00:21:09,081 --> 00:21:09,915
What?

265
00:21:09,998 --> 00:21:11,625
Mechoori, what's that?

266
00:21:21,551 --> 00:21:23,637
-Please do it as fast as you can.
-Yes, sir.

267
00:21:31,228 --> 00:21:33,313
Mu-won, come on out.

268
00:21:33,397 --> 00:21:34,398
Hey.

269
00:21:36,358 --> 00:21:37,192
You're home.

270
00:21:47,160 --> 00:21:47,994
Explain this.

271
00:21:48,078 --> 00:21:49,579
Explain what?

272
00:21:49,663 --> 00:21:51,790
Didn't you see?
They're doing construction.

273
00:21:51,873 --> 00:21:52,874
We're building your lab.

274
00:21:52,958 --> 00:21:54,709
Without even asking me? What is this?

275
00:21:54,793 --> 00:21:56,920
You're the one who changed your number.

276
00:21:57,003 --> 00:21:58,713
I was going to tell you in advance.

277
00:22:00,132 --> 00:22:02,217
I wanted to get it done
while you were at the farm.

278
00:22:02,300 --> 00:22:03,718
I told you I won't do it.

279
00:22:06,012 --> 00:22:08,056
Are you just going to farm here forever?

280
00:22:08,140 --> 00:22:10,183
Is this really the life you wanted?

281
00:22:10,976 --> 00:22:12,519
-Yes.
-No.

282
00:22:13,353 --> 00:22:15,439
You're the happiest when you're in a lab.

283
00:22:19,609 --> 00:22:21,153
-We did it!
-We did it!

284
00:22:21,778 --> 00:22:24,364
-We did it!
-We actually did it!

285
00:22:24,448 --> 00:22:25,907
Finally!

286
00:22:26,533 --> 00:22:28,785
Chang-ho made it big in Bangkok.

287
00:22:28,869 --> 00:22:30,996
He said business suits him
way better than research.

288
00:22:31,079 --> 00:22:33,498
But what about you?
How long are you going to live like this?

289
00:22:34,124 --> 00:22:35,917
I told you.

290
00:22:36,001 --> 00:22:37,752
-I like the way things are now.
-Just wait.

291
00:22:37,836 --> 00:22:41,590
That lab is going to produce
a game changer that will rock Korea.

292
00:22:41,673 --> 00:22:42,716
Sir!

293
00:22:43,717 --> 00:22:45,969
Why can't you understand
what I'm saying? Hey!

294
00:22:52,058 --> 00:22:54,561
Sir… Excuse me!

295
00:22:54,644 --> 00:22:55,562
Yes?

296
00:22:55,645 --> 00:22:57,439
Could you stop for a bit?
How about a break?

297
00:22:57,522 --> 00:22:58,440
-Pardon?
-Take a break.

298
00:22:58,523 --> 00:23:00,317
-Sure.
-Thank you.

299
00:23:00,400 --> 00:23:01,526
Let's take a break.

300
00:23:04,404 --> 00:23:06,031
I seriously can't believe you.

301
00:23:07,657 --> 00:23:11,328
Do you know how many calls
I got from L'Étoile today?

302
00:23:11,411 --> 00:23:12,245
They call nonstop--

303
00:23:16,249 --> 00:23:17,250
L'ÉTOILE CHA JOONG-HOON

304
00:23:17,334 --> 00:23:18,835
It's driving me crazy too.

305
00:23:22,005 --> 00:23:24,883
Meet them again and make it clear
that we won't renew the contract.

306
00:23:24,966 --> 00:23:26,384
You tell them.

307
00:23:27,177 --> 00:23:29,888
If you're half as cold to them
as you are to me, they'll give up.

308
00:23:29,971 --> 00:23:31,056
You do it.

309
00:23:37,145 --> 00:23:38,146
What are you… Hey.

310
00:23:39,439 --> 00:23:40,440
Hello?

311
00:23:45,570 --> 00:23:46,571
Why haven't you left yet?

312
00:23:46,655 --> 00:23:48,448
-I'm leaving now.
-Yes, please go.

313
00:23:51,868 --> 00:23:52,953
Gosh, you scared me.

314
00:23:54,704 --> 00:23:55,705
Hey,

315
00:23:55,789 --> 00:23:57,749
you still don't know who I am?

316
00:23:59,918 --> 00:24:01,670
I'm Kang Mu-won.

317
00:24:02,379 --> 00:24:03,630
Kang Mu-won!

318
00:24:08,593 --> 00:24:10,553
I can't let you go looking like this.

319
00:24:24,526 --> 00:24:25,735
All done.

320
00:24:54,973 --> 00:24:58,601
Why didn't you show me
a perfect suit like this?

321
00:24:58,685 --> 00:25:00,854
It's the same suit

322
00:25:00,937 --> 00:25:02,230
you are wearing.

323
00:25:02,772 --> 00:25:03,690
What?

324
00:25:25,086 --> 00:25:26,338
You're killing it.

325
00:25:29,841 --> 00:25:30,717
Stop!

326
00:25:30,800 --> 00:25:32,260
Please, stop!

327
00:25:35,305 --> 00:25:37,265
Yes, could we please stop now?

328
00:25:37,932 --> 00:25:39,309
I told you there's no need.

329
00:25:39,392 --> 00:25:41,561
-Just take it, will you?
-Mu-won.

330
00:25:42,228 --> 00:25:43,688
Can't I just take a taxi?

331
00:25:43,772 --> 00:25:47,275
Listen. All these little details
are needed to gain the upper hand.

332
00:25:47,359 --> 00:25:50,362
No matter how well you fight,
you can't win a war without weapons…

333
00:25:50,445 --> 00:25:51,446
I'm going to be late.

334
00:25:51,529 --> 00:25:53,114
Hey, wear this instead.

335
00:25:53,198 --> 00:25:54,157
Mu-won.

336
00:25:55,492 --> 00:25:57,869
All right, fine. Then, just take the car.

337
00:26:12,133 --> 00:26:13,301
Nice to meet you.

338
00:26:13,385 --> 00:26:15,970
I'm Gojeuneok Bio's co-CEO, Lee Hae-seok.

339
00:26:16,054 --> 00:26:18,598
Nice to meet you.
I'm Eric Seo from L'Étoile.

340
00:26:21,726 --> 00:26:22,811
I admit that last time,

341
00:26:22,894 --> 00:26:25,063
our order quantity
of raw materials was unreasonable.

342
00:26:25,146 --> 00:26:27,857
This is a revised contract
with the condition

343
00:26:27,941 --> 00:26:30,485
that the raw material supply
will increase gradually.

344
00:26:30,568 --> 00:26:32,112
To increase raw material production,

345
00:26:32,195 --> 00:26:33,863
it also says we will be covering

346
00:26:34,364 --> 00:26:36,157
facility expansion costs and labor costs.

347
00:26:36,241 --> 00:26:40,036
It seems you still don't
fully understand why we won't re-sign.

348
00:26:40,120 --> 00:26:42,455
Gojeuneok's first rule

349
00:26:42,539 --> 00:26:44,958
is for me to have full control
over the entire process.

350
00:26:45,625 --> 00:26:48,378
We cannot continue with a company
that breaks this rule.

351
00:26:48,461 --> 00:26:51,297
With proper facilities and personnel,
I'm sure it will be manageable.

352
00:26:51,381 --> 00:26:54,426
Those things alone can't guarantee
the quality of the materials.

353
00:26:54,509 --> 00:26:56,261
Don't you want more people

354
00:26:56,761 --> 00:26:58,263
to use better quality essence?

355
00:26:59,013 --> 00:27:00,473
That intention may become a mistake.

356
00:27:00,557 --> 00:27:01,724
No, it will become hope.

357
00:27:05,145 --> 00:27:08,356
Hope can help us get started,

358
00:27:08,440 --> 00:27:10,525
but it can't take responsibility
for the outcome.

359
00:27:11,693 --> 00:27:13,486
That reckless optimism

360
00:27:14,237 --> 00:27:15,947
is exactly why we can't work together.

361
00:27:16,030 --> 00:27:19,742
Then, what if we take the same quantity
as our previous contract?

362
00:27:19,826 --> 00:27:21,536
I heard you're preparing to launch on HIT.

363
00:27:21,619 --> 00:27:23,163
We're only selling a limited amount.

364
00:27:23,246 --> 00:27:26,291
I'm sure they'll request
a bigger quantity for the next broadcast.

365
00:27:26,374 --> 00:27:29,461
There's no reason to continue working
with a company that backtracks…

366
00:27:33,006 --> 00:27:34,132
on prior agreements.

367
00:27:39,471 --> 00:27:41,598
I believe I've made myself clear,

368
00:27:41,681 --> 00:27:42,974
so I'll head out.

369
00:27:45,101 --> 00:27:46,686
You sure you won't regret it?

370
00:27:47,896 --> 00:27:49,105
This is L'Étoile.

371
00:27:58,948 --> 00:28:00,867
Maybe I shouldn't have said
that last line.

372
00:28:06,915 --> 00:28:08,875
What did you need to tell me so urgently?

373
00:28:08,958 --> 00:28:10,210
I had something to share.

374
00:28:10,293 --> 00:28:13,046
Gojeuneok Bio has co-CEOs.

375
00:28:13,129 --> 00:28:16,508
Kang Mu-won and Lee Hae-seok.

376
00:28:17,926 --> 00:28:19,010
Lee Hae-seok?

377
00:28:19,093 --> 00:28:21,596
Lee Hae-seok has control
over deciding the contract renewal,

378
00:28:22,180 --> 00:28:23,681
but he's quite firm in his stance.

379
00:28:23,765 --> 00:28:24,724
You met him?

380
00:28:24,807 --> 00:28:26,184
Where is he right now?

381
00:28:27,060 --> 00:28:29,145
He's not someone who's that easy to meet.

382
00:28:29,229 --> 00:28:30,647
Him too?

383
00:28:30,730 --> 00:28:32,607
It's the same with the farm owner.

384
00:28:32,690 --> 00:28:34,734
I failed to meet him so many times.

385
00:28:35,276 --> 00:28:36,444
It seems

386
00:28:36,528 --> 00:28:39,572
people who are very similar to each other
work at Gojeuneok Bio.

387
00:28:43,451 --> 00:28:44,828
Let's go with Plan B now.

388
00:28:44,911 --> 00:28:47,330
If there are two of them,
we need to match their numbers.

389
00:28:47,413 --> 00:28:49,999
I'll try and convince
Mr. Lee Hae-seok from now on.

390
00:28:53,711 --> 00:28:54,712
Mr. Seo?

391
00:28:58,049 --> 00:29:00,802
You really don't recognize me?

392
00:29:02,720 --> 00:29:04,722
You really don't remember me?

393
00:29:08,268 --> 00:29:09,394
I do.

394
00:29:10,895 --> 00:29:12,522
You remember me?

395
00:29:13,898 --> 00:29:15,400
But why did you pretend not to?

396
00:29:16,359 --> 00:29:17,360
Because I felt so sorry.

397
00:29:18,027 --> 00:29:19,821
I felt bad I couldn't be there that day.

398
00:29:21,739 --> 00:29:22,907
You mean

399
00:29:22,991 --> 00:29:25,535
you wanted to come
but you couldn't, right?

400
00:29:25,618 --> 00:29:26,911
Did something happen that day?

401
00:29:29,038 --> 00:29:30,206
Well, it was a long time ago.

402
00:29:31,916 --> 00:29:35,378
Then, how about we chat like back then
until you can remember?

403
00:29:36,754 --> 00:29:37,922
Mr. Seo.

404
00:29:39,757 --> 00:29:42,260
All right. Let's focus on Plan B.

405
00:29:46,431 --> 00:29:49,726
Can't we just find
a different raw material producer?

406
00:29:49,809 --> 00:29:52,395
I talked to headquarters about that too.

407
00:29:52,478 --> 00:29:55,648
But apparently, they tried to farm
white flower noori mushrooms in France

408
00:29:55,732 --> 00:29:56,858
and failed.

409
00:29:56,941 --> 00:29:58,902
And even if they had succeeded,

410
00:29:58,985 --> 00:30:00,904
the process of extracting the ingredients

411
00:30:00,987 --> 00:30:02,697
is Gojeuneok's exclusive technology.

412
00:30:02,780 --> 00:30:05,491
Then, the conclusion is
that they're the only choice.

413
00:30:05,575 --> 00:30:07,285
What did the farm owner say?

414
00:30:07,368 --> 00:30:09,621
Don't get me started.
I didn't even get to meet him.

415
00:30:09,704 --> 00:30:13,458
The workers on the farm there
say he's really strict.

416
00:30:13,541 --> 00:30:15,752
And he seems to hate
communicating with outsiders.

417
00:30:18,087 --> 00:30:19,505
These two people…

418
00:30:19,589 --> 00:30:21,215
They're virtually doppelgängers.

419
00:30:21,299 --> 00:30:22,550
STRICT, DIFFICULT TO REACH

420
00:30:23,301 --> 00:30:24,719
Maybe the same guy?

421
00:30:25,553 --> 00:30:26,387
Mr. Hwang!

422
00:30:26,471 --> 00:30:29,307
-Right?
-What do we do with him?

423
00:30:29,390 --> 00:30:30,475
-That was his best?
-No way.

424
00:30:30,558 --> 00:30:31,559
-That was lame.
-Fire him.

425
00:30:32,602 --> 00:30:34,479
I mean, we can't say it's impossible…

426
00:30:35,730 --> 00:30:36,564
Look.

427
00:30:36,648 --> 00:30:39,567
How can someone manage
the company and the farm at the same time?

428
00:30:39,651 --> 00:30:41,611
Do you think he can just teleport
back and forth?

429
00:30:42,570 --> 00:30:45,573
It's tough to even manage one job,
you know.

430
00:30:45,657 --> 00:30:47,283
I'm having such a hard time right now.

431
00:30:53,206 --> 00:30:55,416
ANYOUNG RICE

432
00:30:58,753 --> 00:30:59,963
Yes.

433
00:31:00,046 --> 00:31:02,507
Anyway, please call me
if there's anything available.

434
00:31:02,590 --> 00:31:07,011
Come on. Weekends don't matter.
I need the money.

435
00:31:07,845 --> 00:31:10,014
Yes. All right, bye.

436
00:31:37,417 --> 00:31:38,626
<i>Use this for baby formula.</i>

437
00:31:45,591 --> 00:31:46,551
Honey?

438
00:31:46,634 --> 00:31:47,969
Hey, it's me.

439
00:31:48,052 --> 00:31:50,304
-Why aren't you coming inside?
-It's nothing. Go on in.

440
00:31:50,388 --> 00:31:53,057
Hey, did you order rice?

441
00:31:53,141 --> 00:31:55,143
Hey, Se-jung. How was your day?

442
00:31:55,226 --> 00:31:58,938
PROUD AND CONFIDENT, DEOKPUNG VILLAGE

443
00:32:26,507 --> 00:32:28,384
I'm sorry for everything.

444
00:32:30,887 --> 00:32:32,263
I…

445
00:32:33,264 --> 00:32:38,061
I was struggling to get by,
and it made me struggle to be generous.

446
00:32:38,895 --> 00:32:43,441
I thought I was all alone in this world
and did a lot of things I was ashamed of.

447
00:32:46,152 --> 00:32:48,988
From now on, I'll stick
to the precise schedule

448
00:32:49,906 --> 00:32:51,199
and I won't speed.

449
00:32:52,241 --> 00:32:57,205
You can tell me whenever you need
to use the restroom before we leave.

450
00:32:58,498 --> 00:32:59,665
Thank you so much!

451
00:33:02,710 --> 00:33:04,837
-Thank you!
-Thank you!

452
00:33:23,523 --> 00:33:25,733
Just think of this
as saving someone's life.

453
00:33:25,817 --> 00:33:27,485
Please help me out just this once.

454
00:33:28,319 --> 00:33:32,740
Ma'am, I'm telling you
I'm really busy right now.

455
00:33:32,824 --> 00:33:35,076
We get the most views
when you appear on our channel!

456
00:33:38,371 --> 00:33:40,623
Hello, HIT subscribers!

457
00:33:40,706 --> 00:33:42,542
I'm home shopping host Dam Ye-jin.

458
00:33:42,625 --> 00:33:46,337
Today, I'll be trying out a day
as a call center agent

459
00:33:46,420 --> 00:33:49,882
to personally hear
the kind of difficulties

460
00:33:49,966 --> 00:33:52,426
our customers actually may have.

461
00:33:52,510 --> 00:33:53,970
All right, shall we go?

462
00:33:55,054 --> 00:33:56,639
Hello, this is--

463
00:33:56,722 --> 00:33:58,474
<i>That shampoo you're selling now…</i>

464
00:33:58,558 --> 00:34:01,769
<i>I only want to buy half of Set 1,</i>
<i>so give me a 50% discount.</i>

465
00:34:01,853 --> 00:34:04,063
Ma'am, I'm really sorry,

466
00:34:04,147 --> 00:34:07,275
but I'm not authorized
to adjust the set or the price.

467
00:34:08,025 --> 00:34:10,486
Wait, you want me to buy something
I can't even use all of?

468
00:34:10,570 --> 00:34:12,321
Are you encouraging
unnecessary consumption?

469
00:34:13,364 --> 00:34:15,575
Hello, how may I help you?

470
00:34:15,658 --> 00:34:17,827
<i>Well, I want to return</i>
<i>the short rib soup I bought.</i>

471
00:34:17,910 --> 00:34:20,496
Was there anything wrong
with the soup you ordered?

472
00:34:20,580 --> 00:34:22,665
<i>I ate it, but it wasn't to my taste.</i>

473
00:34:22,748 --> 00:34:25,126
So you sampled one pack,
but it wasn't to your--

474
00:34:25,209 --> 00:34:26,502
<i>No.</i>

475
00:34:26,586 --> 00:34:28,880
I ate all of them,

476
00:34:28,963 --> 00:34:31,257
but they didn't taste good,
and the bones were too big.

477
00:34:31,340 --> 00:34:32,675
<i>They were so heavy.</i>

478
00:34:32,758 --> 00:34:34,552
You ate everything,
so how can you return--

479
00:34:34,635 --> 00:34:37,972
<i>I said I ate everything!</i>
<i>I didn't leave any!</i>

480
00:34:38,055 --> 00:34:39,599
-Hello--
-<i>You better fix this.</i>

481
00:34:39,682 --> 00:34:40,558
Pardon?

482
00:34:44,520 --> 00:34:46,355
How may I help you, sir?

483
00:34:46,439 --> 00:34:49,609
My family has fallen apart
because of these damn golf shoes.

484
00:34:49,692 --> 00:34:53,070
You ordered
white women's golf shoes in size 235.

485
00:34:53,154 --> 00:34:56,115
Why would you send them
the next morning after my order?

486
00:34:56,199 --> 00:34:57,825
My wife saw these!

487
00:34:57,909 --> 00:34:58,993
-Pardon?
-<i>Forget it.</i>

488
00:34:59,076 --> 00:35:00,703
My wife's filing for divorce,

489
00:35:00,786 --> 00:35:03,706
<i>and I'm going to be bleeding money</i>
<i>with alimony and everything,</i>

490
00:35:03,789 --> 00:35:05,875
<i>so you better compensate me</i>
<i>for emotional distress.</i>

491
00:35:05,958 --> 00:35:07,168
Is he out of his damn…

492
00:35:09,337 --> 00:35:10,838
I can't believe these people.

493
00:35:10,922 --> 00:35:13,090
Excuse me, Ms. Dam?

494
00:35:13,799 --> 00:35:17,261
Could you please just take
one call smoothly?

495
00:35:19,347 --> 00:35:20,389
Sorry.

496
00:35:23,059 --> 00:35:24,769
I'll do a proper call this time.

497
00:35:24,852 --> 00:35:26,187
I will now be a yes-man.

498
00:35:26,270 --> 00:35:27,813
-Yes-man.
-Yes-man.

499
00:35:27,897 --> 00:35:28,856
That's right.

500
00:35:28,940 --> 00:35:30,149
Yes! Yes!

501
00:35:30,233 --> 00:35:32,485
And there's a call right on time.
Let's get into it.

502
00:35:32,568 --> 00:35:34,695
Hello, this is Dam Ye-jin,
your agent for today--

503
00:35:34,779 --> 00:35:36,072
<i>-Is this HIT?</i>
-Yes, it is.

504
00:35:36,155 --> 00:35:37,990
<i>How can you sell</i>
<i>a ridiculous item like this?</i>

505
00:35:40,826 --> 00:35:43,079
Is there something wrong
with the item you purchased?

506
00:35:43,162 --> 00:35:45,414
Don't you have a quality control team?

507
00:35:45,957 --> 00:35:48,834
You shipped out something
that doesn't even work properly.

508
00:35:48,918 --> 00:35:50,586
This is how you handle things?

509
00:35:50,670 --> 00:35:52,672
You're using that
as a drying rack for laundry?

510
00:35:52,755 --> 00:35:56,592
No matter how long I sit in there,
I don't sweat at all.

511
00:35:56,676 --> 00:35:57,635
Is it broken?

512
00:35:57,718 --> 00:35:59,428
This was so expensive.

513
00:35:59,512 --> 00:36:02,348
Gosh, it's giving me a headache.

514
00:36:04,225 --> 00:36:07,311
Whatever's wrong with it,
it's just an expensive wooden chair now.

515
00:36:07,395 --> 00:36:08,312
I see.

516
00:36:08,396 --> 00:36:11,065
You trusted home shopping host
Dam Ye-jin and bought it,

517
00:36:11,148 --> 00:36:13,734
<i>-but there was an issue--</i>
-I've never trusted Dam Ye-jin.

518
00:36:13,818 --> 00:36:14,986
I'm very disappointed though.

519
00:36:15,069 --> 00:36:16,904
I see.

520
00:36:16,988 --> 00:36:17,947
Please wait one moment.

521
00:36:24,120 --> 00:36:25,913
Excuse me, sir,

522
00:36:26,414 --> 00:36:29,875
but could you tell me your name
so I can check your purchase information?

523
00:36:32,253 --> 00:36:33,170
It's Lee Hae-seok.

524
00:36:33,254 --> 00:36:34,171
DEOKPUNG VILLAGE

525
00:36:34,255 --> 00:36:35,756
<i>It's Lee Hae-seok.</i>

526
00:36:36,507 --> 00:36:38,092
<i>Gojeuneok Bio has co-CEOs.</i>

527
00:36:38,175 --> 00:36:40,970
Kang Mu-won and Lee Hae-seok.

528
00:36:41,554 --> 00:36:42,388
<i>These two people…</i>

529
00:36:42,471 --> 00:36:44,557
They're virtually doppelgängers.
Maybe the same guy?

530
00:36:44,640 --> 00:36:45,683
<i>Him too?</i>

531
00:36:45,766 --> 00:36:47,184
<i>It's the same with the farm owner.</i>

532
00:36:47,268 --> 00:36:48,894
<i>I failed to meet him so many times.</i>

533
00:36:48,978 --> 00:36:50,771
Mr. "Lee something Seok"? Mr. Lee!

534
00:36:50,855 --> 00:36:52,898
For privacy reasons,
the middle character is hidden.

535
00:36:52,982 --> 00:36:54,817
-What's your full name?
-It's Matthew.

536
00:36:55,735 --> 00:36:57,194
<i>Gojeuneok Bio has co-CEOs.</i>

537
00:36:57,278 --> 00:36:58,779
<i>The farm owner… "Lee something Seok"…</i>

538
00:36:58,863 --> 00:36:59,822
<i>It's Lee Hae-seok.</i>

539
00:37:01,449 --> 00:37:02,366
FARM OWNER

540
00:37:08,289 --> 00:37:10,041
LEE HAE-SEOK

541
00:37:10,791 --> 00:37:13,085
<i>It's Lee Hae-seok.</i>

542
00:37:17,548 --> 00:37:19,383
Sir, can you wait just one moment?

543
00:37:20,926 --> 00:37:23,888
Tell him the staff in charge
will come in person to take care of it.

544
00:37:29,518 --> 00:37:32,313
Seriously, thank you so much.

545
00:37:32,396 --> 00:37:33,439
Thank you!

546
00:37:43,783 --> 00:37:46,535
Hit or push through my car if you want.

547
00:37:46,619 --> 00:37:47,703
No!

548
00:37:47,787 --> 00:37:51,749
I've had men follow me in their sports
cars before, but a tractor is a first.

549
00:37:51,832 --> 00:37:53,209
It's pretty unique.

550
00:37:53,292 --> 00:37:55,920
I guess "Mechoori" means Matthew Lee,

551
00:37:56,003 --> 00:37:57,671
not "mechoori" as in quail.

552
00:38:00,341 --> 00:38:02,885
That jerk.

553
00:38:05,679 --> 00:38:07,932
Ye-jin! You must've lost your mind!

554
00:38:08,015 --> 00:38:08,974
I must've been crazy!

555
00:38:09,558 --> 00:38:11,060
Wait. I can make it up to him.

556
00:38:11,143 --> 00:38:12,228
Can I?

557
00:38:12,311 --> 00:38:13,145
I can.

558
00:38:14,563 --> 00:38:16,232
I don't think I can.

559
00:38:16,315 --> 00:38:18,234
No, I have to.

560
00:38:18,317 --> 00:38:19,735
I have to.

561
00:38:19,819 --> 00:38:20,945
I must.

562
00:38:21,028 --> 00:38:22,363
I can do it.

563
00:38:22,446 --> 00:38:23,280
Right.

564
00:38:23,364 --> 00:38:24,490
Let's give it a try.

565
00:38:56,480 --> 00:38:58,649
Hello!

566
00:38:58,732 --> 00:39:00,776
It's nice to see you again.

567
00:39:07,992 --> 00:39:09,201
Did you forget the agreement?

568
00:39:09,285 --> 00:39:10,786
I'm here today because you called me.

569
00:39:10,870 --> 00:39:12,163
I'm your call center agent.

570
00:39:15,499 --> 00:39:17,751
Just give me the number
for the staff in charge.

571
00:39:23,674 --> 00:39:24,550
HIT
DAM YE-JIN

572
00:39:26,677 --> 00:39:28,262
-Are you kidding me?
-What?

573
00:39:28,345 --> 00:39:30,973
I sold the products,
so I'm the staff in charge.

574
00:39:32,391 --> 00:39:34,435
Where's your bathtub, sir?

575
00:39:35,978 --> 00:39:37,438
Fine. Go take a look,

576
00:39:38,731 --> 00:39:39,857
Ms. Dam.

577
00:39:40,691 --> 00:39:43,235
Yes, sir! I'll make my way in!

578
00:39:59,251 --> 00:40:01,170
I ran a detailed inspection,

579
00:40:01,253 --> 00:40:02,880
and it's not broken.

580
00:40:02,963 --> 00:40:05,174
It was just operator error, sir.

581
00:40:05,257 --> 00:40:06,842
<i>This blanket</i>

582
00:40:06,926 --> 00:40:08,969
<i>will be included for preheating.</i>

583
00:40:09,053 --> 00:40:13,432
<i>Cover the top with this blanket,</i>
<i>turn the power on, and wait 20 minutes.</i>

584
00:40:13,516 --> 00:40:14,850
<i>Please keep this in mind.</i>

585
00:40:14,934 --> 00:40:16,060
I explained

586
00:40:16,143 --> 00:40:19,522
that you have to cover it
with this blanket to preheat it.

587
00:40:19,605 --> 00:40:23,108
I emphasized it several times,
but I guess you didn't listen.

588
00:40:24,944 --> 00:40:26,362
You can't just insist it's working.

589
00:40:26,445 --> 00:40:27,530
"Insist"?

590
00:40:28,155 --> 00:40:29,698
Then, did you think

591
00:40:29,782 --> 00:40:32,576
we sent this blanket
as a meaningless freebie?

592
00:40:33,494 --> 00:40:37,665
Are you embarrassed because you complained
that a perfectly fine machine was broken?

593
00:40:38,290 --> 00:40:39,500
Seriously?

594
00:40:40,125 --> 00:40:41,585
It doesn't make you sweat!

595
00:40:44,547 --> 00:40:46,006
There's no need to explain.

596
00:40:46,090 --> 00:40:48,425
I'll just show you
whether you sweat or not.

597
00:40:49,510 --> 00:40:50,803
Open that too.

598
00:40:51,554 --> 00:40:53,931
Don't file another complaint later
saying that's broken too.

599
00:40:55,349 --> 00:40:57,643
Fine. We'll open that too.

600
00:40:59,144 --> 00:41:01,689
It's already hot and steamy
with the preheating, isn't it?

601
00:41:02,815 --> 00:41:05,025
It's not nearly hot enough to sweat.

602
00:41:05,776 --> 00:41:06,610
You better hope so.

603
00:41:10,990 --> 00:41:12,241
Hold on a minute.

604
00:41:12,825 --> 00:41:13,951
What are you doing?

605
00:41:14,034 --> 00:41:15,536
What?

606
00:41:15,619 --> 00:41:18,372
You're pressing pressure points
that help you sweat.

607
00:41:19,081 --> 00:41:20,666
You think those tricks will fool me?

608
00:41:21,584 --> 00:41:24,253
If massaging your temples caused sweat,
all saunas would disappear.

609
00:41:24,336 --> 00:41:27,506
I work on little sleep and suffer
from headaches due to such bias.

610
00:41:34,221 --> 00:41:35,639
You're sweating!

611
00:41:35,723 --> 00:41:38,434
See? You're sweating! Right there!

612
00:41:42,730 --> 00:41:43,814
The ceiling's leaking.

613
00:41:43,897 --> 00:41:46,150
The ceiling? Why?
It looks completely fine.

614
00:41:46,233 --> 00:41:47,568
Mr. Mechoori, look here.

615
00:41:47,651 --> 00:41:48,986
Look here, not the ceiling.

616
00:41:49,069 --> 00:41:51,113
Mr. Mechoori!

617
00:41:51,196 --> 00:41:52,698
You see all this sweat forming here?

618
00:41:53,490 --> 00:41:54,575
My house is usually hot.

619
00:41:57,328 --> 00:41:58,329
Raise your arms.

620
00:41:59,121 --> 00:42:00,831
-What?
-Raise your arms.

621
00:42:01,540 --> 00:42:02,374
Why?

622
00:42:04,543 --> 00:42:05,836
What?

623
00:42:05,919 --> 00:42:08,005
-Mr. Mechoori, let me see your arms.
-Why?

624
00:42:08,088 --> 00:42:09,506
Come on. I need to check something.

625
00:42:09,590 --> 00:42:11,550
-Check what?
-Just raise them once.

626
00:42:11,634 --> 00:42:12,760
-For what?
-Just one minute.

627
00:42:12,843 --> 00:42:14,303
-Go away.
-It's over for you.

628
00:42:14,386 --> 00:42:16,972
-I got you. Raise your arms.
-Hey, what are you…

629
00:42:17,056 --> 00:42:18,015
Sit. Raise your arms.

630
00:42:18,599 --> 00:42:19,850
Ms. Dam!

631
00:42:19,933 --> 00:42:21,143
Tickle, tickle!

632
00:42:21,226 --> 00:42:22,061
Ms. Dam!

633
00:42:22,144 --> 00:42:23,228
-What?
-Wait…

634
00:42:24,104 --> 00:42:24,980
Okay, fine!

635
00:42:25,064 --> 00:42:26,940
-I take back my complaint!
-No, it's too late.

636
00:42:27,024 --> 00:42:28,525
-I need to see--
-Ms. Dam!

637
00:42:47,044 --> 00:42:49,463
TEMPERATURE

638
00:42:49,546 --> 00:42:51,298
ERROR

639
00:43:01,141 --> 00:43:03,018
I guess you were a bit embarrassed,

640
00:43:03,102 --> 00:43:04,728
seeing how you even gave me tea.

641
00:43:05,938 --> 00:43:08,774
If you're not going to drink it, then go.
Our business is over.

642
00:43:09,733 --> 00:43:12,569
How long are you going to
keep playing dumb for?

643
00:43:13,237 --> 00:43:16,281
You think I came all the way here
just to check on the product?

644
00:43:16,365 --> 00:43:17,950
Don't look down on HIT's QC team.

645
00:43:18,033 --> 00:43:19,618
You're the one who overreacted.

646
00:43:20,244 --> 00:43:22,037
I simply made a call
to the service center.

647
00:43:22,996 --> 00:43:24,081
That's what I mean.

648
00:43:25,124 --> 00:43:28,043
Don't you get why I overreacted?

649
00:43:30,921 --> 00:43:32,589
Let me formally introduce myself,

650
00:43:32,673 --> 00:43:34,591
Mr. Lee Hae-seok.

651
00:43:39,680 --> 00:43:42,850
I'll see you again, Mr. Lee!

652
00:43:51,316 --> 00:43:52,443
Changsik.

653
00:43:53,152 --> 00:43:54,445
Changsik!

654
00:43:54,528 --> 00:43:55,904
Hey, Changsik.

655
00:43:57,948 --> 00:43:59,992
Are you ignoring me too?

656
00:44:01,952 --> 00:44:02,995
Give me your paw.

657
00:44:03,787 --> 00:44:06,290
Hey, I'm feeling really down today.
Come on.

658
00:44:07,458 --> 00:44:09,001
Just once, Changsik.

659
00:44:09,084 --> 00:44:09,918
Give me your paw!

660
00:44:11,712 --> 00:44:14,506
Hey, come on. Give me your paw.

661
00:44:14,590 --> 00:44:15,841
Hey.

662
00:44:15,924 --> 00:44:18,469
-Ma'am.
-Give this to him.

663
00:44:21,472 --> 00:44:23,515
Hey, whether it's a dog or a human,

664
00:44:23,599 --> 00:44:26,810
they say you should feed them
before telling them what to do.

665
00:44:26,894 --> 00:44:30,147
If you want him to listen to you,
you need to feed him first.

666
00:44:31,732 --> 00:44:32,775
Right.

667
00:44:33,692 --> 00:44:35,319
I need to feed him first.

668
00:44:36,779 --> 00:44:37,780
Changsik, here.

669
00:44:42,743 --> 00:44:44,787
What would he like then?

670
00:44:46,705 --> 00:44:48,999
That's right! Your bathtub, ma'am.

671
00:44:49,875 --> 00:44:52,669
I got a call from Mechoori.
He said it's fine.

672
00:44:53,754 --> 00:44:55,506
You came all the way here for nothing.

673
00:44:55,589 --> 00:44:58,967
It's fine. I came for other reasons too.
And I was missing your potatoes.

674
00:45:00,385 --> 00:45:02,137
You want some potatoes before you go?

675
00:45:02,221 --> 00:45:05,307
Ma'am, if you keep asking me
to stay overnight like this…

676
00:45:05,933 --> 00:45:07,184
Sure!

677
00:45:10,729 --> 00:45:11,730
FARMING LOG

678
00:46:47,367 --> 00:46:48,619
Are you up?

679
00:46:49,202 --> 00:46:51,913
Yes. Are you going somewhere?

680
00:46:51,997 --> 00:46:55,125
I'm going to the mushroom farm.
They're short-handed.

681
00:46:57,169 --> 00:46:58,754
-Where?
-The mushroom farm.

682
00:47:34,539 --> 00:47:35,457
Did you sleep well?

683
00:47:36,416 --> 00:47:37,542
The weather's so nice.

684
00:47:37,626 --> 00:47:38,710
-Good morning.
-Hi.

685
00:47:39,294 --> 00:47:40,921
-Hello.
-Hi.

686
00:47:42,047 --> 00:47:42,964
-Good morning.
-Hey.

687
00:47:43,048 --> 00:47:44,633
-Good morning. Did you sleep well?
-Yes.

688
00:47:55,894 --> 00:47:56,937
Ms. Dam?

689
00:47:58,021 --> 00:47:59,147
How did you know?

690
00:48:01,149 --> 00:48:02,192
Well,

691
00:48:02,859 --> 00:48:04,486
I guess farming clothes

692
00:48:04,569 --> 00:48:06,071
can't hide my beauty.

693
00:48:08,365 --> 00:48:09,616
Right…

694
00:48:10,450 --> 00:48:11,993
This is my last warning.

695
00:48:12,077 --> 00:48:13,537
Please, just leave.

696
00:48:14,287 --> 00:48:16,123
Sweetie, come here!

697
00:48:16,206 --> 00:48:17,666
Yes, ma'am!

698
00:48:17,749 --> 00:48:18,959
She's calling me.

699
00:48:19,042 --> 00:48:20,001
Wait…

700
00:48:20,919 --> 00:48:22,379
I'm coming!

701
00:48:28,552 --> 00:48:35,350
Deokpung's pride and treasure,
the white flower noori mushrooms!

702
00:48:35,976 --> 00:48:41,898
As always,
please handle each one with care!

703
00:48:41,982 --> 00:48:43,150
Come on!

704
00:48:43,233 --> 00:48:44,276
Let's go!

705
00:48:44,359 --> 00:48:46,528
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

706
00:49:04,713 --> 00:49:06,548
We're getting off work right on the dot.

707
00:49:06,631 --> 00:49:08,091
-That's right!
-On the dot!

708
00:49:08,175 --> 00:49:10,635
Our work is not over yet!

709
00:49:10,719 --> 00:49:11,595
Deokpung's--

710
00:49:11,678 --> 00:49:13,096
Let's go!

711
00:49:13,180 --> 00:49:14,765
Make sure to wrap up for us!

712
00:49:16,558 --> 00:49:17,934
See you!

713
00:49:26,860 --> 00:49:27,694
Good work today.

714
00:49:28,820 --> 00:49:29,654
Right.

715
00:49:34,326 --> 00:49:37,829
I'm going through all this effort,
so could you please spare me some time?

716
00:49:37,913 --> 00:49:39,706
Did you review the materials I left you?

717
00:49:40,874 --> 00:49:41,708
No.

718
00:49:42,417 --> 00:49:44,795
Then, just give me ten… No, five minutes.

719
00:49:44,878 --> 00:49:46,630
Give me five minutes, and I'll brief you.

720
00:49:46,713 --> 00:49:47,547
It's fine.

721
00:49:47,631 --> 00:49:50,926
Can't you reconsider
and renew the contract?

722
00:49:51,009 --> 00:49:53,804
L'Étoile said they'll just accept
the quantity you can produce,

723
00:49:53,887 --> 00:49:55,972
so there's no issue now.

724
00:49:56,056 --> 00:49:57,891
They already broke our trust.

725
00:49:57,974 --> 00:50:01,269
We can't work with people
who have already broken their promise.

726
00:50:01,353 --> 00:50:02,729
Are you a robot or something?

727
00:50:02,813 --> 00:50:04,481
Business is done by people.

728
00:50:04,564 --> 00:50:06,316
It can't be perfect all the time.

729
00:50:06,399 --> 00:50:07,818
Ms. Dam.

730
00:50:09,194 --> 00:50:11,696
Can you put spilled milk
back in the glass?

731
00:50:12,447 --> 00:50:15,325
Look, I'm saying
we can quickly wipe it with a towel.

732
00:50:15,408 --> 00:50:16,576
And if we dry it in the sun

733
00:50:17,244 --> 00:50:18,912
and squeeze it out, we can reuse it.

734
00:50:18,995 --> 00:50:21,122
If it's not dried properly,
it'll get moldy.

735
00:50:21,206 --> 00:50:23,708
That's what we call contamination.
All right?

736
00:50:29,256 --> 00:50:31,049
I understand what you're saying,

737
00:50:31,132 --> 00:50:33,051
but if you could just reconsider…

738
00:50:33,134 --> 00:50:35,929
I'm practically pleading, sir. Please?

739
00:50:36,012 --> 00:50:38,473
If we discuss this further,
you might change your mind…

740
00:50:38,557 --> 00:50:40,308
My hand!

741
00:50:40,392 --> 00:50:42,686
My hand was almost caught in the gate.

742
00:50:46,022 --> 00:50:47,983
If you take one step inside,

743
00:50:48,066 --> 00:50:49,693
I'll immediately call the police.

744
00:50:55,073 --> 00:50:56,199
Ms. Dam!

745
00:50:56,283 --> 00:50:59,661
Hey, we even did a sauna session together.
You're so mean.

746
00:50:59,744 --> 00:51:01,079
Will you please leave?

747
00:51:01,955 --> 00:51:03,039
I will but…

748
00:51:03,665 --> 00:51:04,624
What are you doing?

749
00:51:04,708 --> 00:51:06,668
-I'll leave, but if we could talk…
-Hey…

750
00:51:06,751 --> 00:51:09,337
-You're using force?
-You're the one pushing right now.

751
00:51:09,421 --> 00:51:11,131
Just a moment. Please, sir.

752
00:51:11,214 --> 00:51:12,716
-Ms. Dam!
-Mr. Lee.

753
00:51:13,258 --> 00:51:14,885
Mr. Lee!

754
00:51:22,475 --> 00:51:23,310
"IN"

755
00:51:23,393 --> 00:51:24,352
CHARACTER FOR "PERSON"

756
00:51:24,436 --> 00:51:26,062
DERIVED FROM PEOPLE
LEANING ON EACH OTHER

757
00:51:31,109 --> 00:51:32,277
Please get off me.

758
00:51:35,822 --> 00:51:36,948
No, don't come in. Get out.

759
00:51:37,032 --> 00:51:39,034
I'm going to!

760
00:51:40,535 --> 00:51:41,745
For crying out loud.

761
00:51:58,136 --> 00:51:58,970
Ms. Dam?

762
00:52:03,183 --> 00:52:04,184
Hang on…

763
00:52:10,982 --> 00:52:13,652
I do understand your decision, Mr. Lee.

764
00:52:13,735 --> 00:52:15,320
But that makes me want this more.

765
00:52:15,403 --> 00:52:17,072
I really want to introduce an essence

766
00:52:17,155 --> 00:52:19,324
made with good ingredients
to our customers.

767
00:52:21,159 --> 00:52:23,453
Gosh, talking all by myself
is making my mouth hurt.

768
00:52:23,536 --> 00:52:24,663
Oh, dear.

769
00:52:27,123 --> 00:52:28,500
Give it a rest.

770
00:52:28,583 --> 00:52:30,418
It really hurts.
What if it's broken forever?

771
00:52:32,629 --> 00:52:33,797
It's hurting so much.

772
00:52:35,590 --> 00:52:37,801
Okay, it's all done.

773
00:52:37,884 --> 00:52:41,054
It's not good if it gets wet,
so be careful.

774
00:52:41,137 --> 00:52:45,058
Is it okay to take this off
just for a moment this evening?

775
00:52:45,558 --> 00:52:46,393
Sorry?

776
00:52:47,394 --> 00:52:50,146
WOORI DEOKPUNG MEDICAL CLINIC

777
00:52:54,651 --> 00:52:56,945
Why did you have to fall
so dramatically like that?

778
00:52:57,028 --> 00:52:58,989
Were you trying
to blackmail me with an injury?

779
00:53:00,740 --> 00:53:04,703
If I was going to use such tacky methods,
I would've used my beauty first.

780
00:53:04,786 --> 00:53:05,954
So,

781
00:53:06,496 --> 00:53:08,123
should I change my tactics then?

782
00:53:13,586 --> 00:53:15,755
I have a live broadcast at 11:00 p.m.

783
00:53:16,506 --> 00:53:19,884
I can't let my injury stand out
more than the product.

784
00:53:20,885 --> 00:53:23,179
I've prepared so hard for that item too.

785
00:53:29,019 --> 00:53:30,103
It's this way.

786
00:53:46,077 --> 00:53:47,662
<i>I have a live broadcast at 11:00 p.m.</i>

787
00:53:47,746 --> 00:53:51,458
I can't let my injury stand out
more than the product.

788
00:54:03,678 --> 00:54:05,513
HIT

789
00:54:05,597 --> 00:54:07,849
<i>If you look here,</i>
<i>you can adjust the resistance.</i>

790
00:54:07,932 --> 00:54:09,476
<i>Whether beginner or expert,</i>

791
00:54:09,559 --> 00:54:12,479
<i>you can tailor your workout</i>
<i>to match your fitness level.</i>

792
00:54:12,562 --> 00:54:13,980
<i>After you adjust it,</i>

793
00:54:14,064 --> 00:54:18,693
<i>grab the bar,</i>
<i>pull it all the way back, and that's it.</i>

794
00:54:18,777 --> 00:54:21,529
<i>You'll get both cardio</i>
<i>and strength training in one go.</i>

795
00:54:21,613 --> 00:54:23,531
<i>Then, push all the way out with your legs.</i>

796
00:54:23,615 --> 00:54:29,996
<i>You have to pull the bar all the way back</i>
<i>toward your upper abdomen</i>

797
00:54:30,080 --> 00:54:32,248
<i>to maximize your workout.</i>

798
00:54:32,332 --> 00:54:33,458
That must hurt…

799
00:54:33,541 --> 00:54:36,753
<i>It really feels like</i>
<i>you're rowing on water.</i>

800
00:54:37,337 --> 00:54:40,715
<i>There's strong resistance when you pull.</i>

801
00:54:44,803 --> 00:54:45,970
<i>That makes me want this more.</i>

802
00:54:46,054 --> 00:54:47,722
I really want to introduce an essence

803
00:54:47,806 --> 00:54:49,933
made with good ingredients
to our customers.

804
00:54:59,609 --> 00:55:01,236
HIT HOMESHOPPING
DAM YE-JIN

805
00:55:14,499 --> 00:55:15,583
Jin-yi.

806
00:55:16,334 --> 00:55:17,919
What are you doing here at this hour--

807
00:55:19,754 --> 00:55:21,756
You're such a negligent landlord.

808
00:55:22,507 --> 00:55:24,968
Your tenant wasn't paying rent,
but you didn't press them.

809
00:55:26,386 --> 00:55:27,428
I said you didn't have to.

810
00:55:27,512 --> 00:55:29,430
And I told you hundreds of times

811
00:55:30,181 --> 00:55:31,891
I refuse to be treated
like a charity case.

812
00:55:36,062 --> 00:55:36,980
What about Som-yi?

813
00:55:37,063 --> 00:55:39,440
She's busy bragging about the gift
that someone left her.

814
00:55:42,485 --> 00:55:43,486
What was she doing here?

815
00:55:50,326 --> 00:55:51,327
It's nothing.

816
00:55:53,413 --> 00:55:54,414
Nothing?

817
00:55:59,419 --> 00:56:00,461
Hey.

818
00:56:03,089 --> 00:56:04,465
What is it this time?

819
00:56:04,549 --> 00:56:07,719
The Beauty Song essence that Ms. Song's
been preparing for three years…

820
00:56:07,802 --> 00:56:08,636
It's launching soon.

821
00:56:09,429 --> 00:56:11,055
Customers won't buy essence again

822
00:56:11,139 --> 00:56:12,765
a week after buying L'Étoile's essence.

823
00:56:12,849 --> 00:56:14,809
They will if it's good.

824
00:56:15,476 --> 00:56:17,520
You should be focusing
on the product's quality.

825
00:56:18,980 --> 00:56:22,525
Are you really that bent
on dragging Ms. Song down?

826
00:56:27,405 --> 00:56:28,406
Poor Ms. Song.

827
00:56:29,699 --> 00:56:32,076
You really are cruel. Geez.

828
00:56:38,208 --> 00:56:40,251
HIT HOMESHOPPING
DAM YE-JIN

829
00:56:55,600 --> 00:56:58,811
Mu-won, let's end things
with L'Étoile for good.

830
00:57:01,105 --> 00:57:03,358
Send me the list of other clients.

831
00:57:14,953 --> 00:57:18,164
PERILLA LEAVES, BELLFLOWER ROOT,
MEAT PATTIES, STUFFED CUCUMBER KIMCHI

832
00:57:19,999 --> 00:57:22,210
YOU MUST BE BUSY

833
00:57:35,890 --> 00:57:37,058
Welcome back.

834
00:57:37,642 --> 00:57:38,643
Did you eat dinner yet?

835
00:57:40,353 --> 00:57:41,521
I don't have an appetite.

836
00:57:44,607 --> 00:57:45,733
You haven't eaten, have you?

837
00:57:45,817 --> 00:57:48,528
-Come here, I'll make you--
-Please, just…

838
00:57:48,611 --> 00:57:49,988
What's wrong? Are you hurt?

839
00:57:52,031 --> 00:57:53,241
It's nothing.

840
00:57:54,409 --> 00:57:55,243
What about dinner?

841
00:57:55,326 --> 00:57:56,536
Geez.

842
00:57:56,619 --> 00:57:58,830
Can't you stop nagging me about my meals?

843
00:57:59,539 --> 00:58:01,291
I told you a million times I can't eat.

844
00:58:01,374 --> 00:58:03,293
I don't have the time!

845
00:58:03,376 --> 00:58:05,962
Why do you keep giving me food
that I'll end up throwing away?

846
00:58:06,045 --> 00:58:07,463
It just makes me feel bad.

847
00:58:11,301 --> 00:58:13,344
It's okay if you throw them all away.

848
00:58:13,428 --> 00:58:16,598
I just don't want your fridge to be empty

849
00:58:16,681 --> 00:58:18,391
when you want to eat something.

850
00:58:19,434 --> 00:58:20,435
Geez…

851
00:58:22,353 --> 00:58:24,689
You shouldn't just barge in here, Dad.

852
00:58:25,315 --> 00:58:26,524
I'm not a kid.

853
00:58:27,358 --> 00:58:30,695
I told you,
I don't need stuff like this right now!

854
00:58:34,157 --> 00:58:35,533
Why do you always…

855
00:58:37,327 --> 00:58:39,037
just do as you please?

856
00:58:45,293 --> 00:58:46,336
Ye-jin.

857
00:58:47,378 --> 00:58:49,505
Please, don't do this.

858
00:58:50,256 --> 00:58:51,257
But it's true.

859
00:58:52,133 --> 00:58:53,760
Mom abandoned me.

860
00:58:54,969 --> 00:58:57,180
-Ye-jin.
-I don't care anymore.

861
00:58:57,847 --> 00:58:59,432
I'm going to tell everyone.

862
00:58:59,515 --> 00:59:01,601
I'm going to tell them
Song Myeong-hwa's my mom

863
00:59:01,684 --> 00:59:03,353
and that she's a liar.

864
00:59:05,021 --> 00:59:06,981
I told her not to contact you!

865
00:59:11,110 --> 00:59:12,236
What?

866
00:59:13,696 --> 00:59:17,033
Your mom actually did call.

867
00:59:17,992 --> 00:59:19,702
She said she was so startled then,

868
00:59:19,786 --> 00:59:22,038
and she wanted to apologize to you.

869
00:59:22,121 --> 00:59:22,955
But,

870
00:59:23,873 --> 00:59:24,791
I can't…

871
00:59:26,542 --> 00:59:29,671
see you get hurt like that again.

872
00:59:30,463 --> 00:59:33,383
So I told her not to contact you again.

873
00:59:33,466 --> 00:59:35,093
I'm the one who stopped her.

874
00:59:35,176 --> 00:59:36,010
Why?

875
00:59:37,303 --> 00:59:38,554
Why did you do that?

876
00:59:40,223 --> 00:59:41,307
What about me?

877
00:59:42,725 --> 00:59:45,603
Why decide that on your own?
Who are you to stop her?

878
00:59:48,564 --> 00:59:49,565
I'm sorry.

879
00:59:54,570 --> 00:59:55,655
I'm really sorry.

880
01:00:11,254 --> 01:00:12,255
Sorry.

881
01:00:15,341 --> 01:00:16,634
I'm really sorry.

882
01:01:10,563 --> 01:01:14,400
GOJEUNEOK BIO

883
01:01:33,461 --> 01:01:34,754
Hello?

884
01:01:34,837 --> 01:01:36,339
<i>Mom.</i>

885
01:01:38,841 --> 01:01:39,967
Excuse me.

886
01:01:40,051 --> 01:01:42,178
-I clearly told you--
<i>-It's me, Ye-jin.</i>

887
01:01:45,264 --> 01:01:46,265
What?

888
01:01:48,059 --> 01:01:49,310
Who did you say you were?

889
01:01:49,852 --> 01:01:51,103
<i>Did you see my show?</i>

890
01:01:53,022 --> 01:01:56,567
<i>Actually, I got hurt today.</i>

891
01:02:02,657 --> 01:02:05,076
3 MISSED CALLS

892
01:02:09,121 --> 01:02:10,957
<i>Whenever I moved,</i>

893
01:02:12,291 --> 01:02:13,835
it hurt so much,

894
01:02:15,711 --> 01:02:17,880
so I just didn't care…

895
01:02:19,549 --> 01:02:21,843
and wanted to quit the show.

896
01:02:24,303 --> 01:02:25,513
But I held it in.

897
01:02:29,892 --> 01:02:31,644
Didn't I do a good job, Mom?

898
01:02:32,436 --> 01:02:34,146
<i>I'm a pro, aren't I?</i>

899
01:02:34,230 --> 01:02:35,523
Ms. Dam.

900
01:02:35,606 --> 01:02:36,941
Are you drunk?

901
01:02:37,024 --> 01:02:37,984
<i>But…</i>

902
01:02:39,986 --> 01:02:41,487
today…

903
01:02:45,032 --> 01:02:46,409
I guess I was pretty stressed.

904
01:02:48,119 --> 01:02:51,122
<i>I took my anger out on Dad for no reason.</i>

905
01:02:51,205 --> 01:02:52,748
Hang up before you embarrass yourself.

906
01:02:52,832 --> 01:02:54,041
<i>I'm pathetic,</i>

907
01:02:54,792 --> 01:02:56,002
<i>aren't I?</i>

908
01:02:56,085 --> 01:02:57,628
I'm hanging up.

909
01:03:00,089 --> 01:03:01,257
Hello?

910
01:03:01,340 --> 01:03:03,217
Ms. Dam!

911
01:03:13,185 --> 01:03:15,229
<i>The person you are calling is unavailable.</i>

912
01:03:27,366 --> 01:03:28,451
<i>Mom…</i>

913
01:03:31,412 --> 01:03:32,914
I miss you,

914
01:03:34,123 --> 01:03:35,374
Mom.

915
01:03:54,685 --> 01:03:55,686
I'm bleeding.

916
01:04:25,383 --> 01:04:29,303
SCHOOL ZONE

917
01:04:45,653 --> 01:04:48,531
CONVENIENCE STORE

918
01:05:48,674 --> 01:05:50,468
SOLD OUT ON YOU

919
01:05:50,551 --> 01:05:56,474
THANKS TO SPECIAL GUEST AHN SANG-WOO

920
01:06:20,623 --> 01:06:22,625
<i>Are you curious whether she slept well</i>

921
01:06:22,708 --> 01:06:26,253
<i>or if she made sure to eat her meals?</i>

922
01:06:26,337 --> 01:06:28,214
<i>Are talks going smoothly</i>
<i>with Gojeuneok Bio?</i>

923
01:06:28,297 --> 01:06:30,132
It's been a long time, Mr. Lee.

924
01:06:30,216 --> 01:06:33,219
<i>Whatever you do,</i>
<i>nothing's going to change.</i>

925
01:06:33,302 --> 01:06:35,179
He won't buy the corn?

926
01:06:35,262 --> 01:06:38,641
<i>All this corn might go to waste.</i>

927
01:06:38,724 --> 01:06:40,017
This has nothing to do with you.

928
01:06:40,101 --> 01:06:41,143
-Let's sell them.
-What?

929
01:06:41,227 --> 01:06:43,854
<i>Let's sell them through a livestream.</i>

930
01:06:43,938 --> 01:06:46,857
Hello, everyone.
I'm home shopping host Dam Ye-jin.

931
01:06:46,941 --> 01:06:49,360
<i>Ms. Dam, stay still.</i>

932
01:06:58,035 --> 01:07:00,037
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park

